Florence is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 only (GPL-2.0-only).
The full text is in LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt. There is no "or any later version" clause.

Why version 2 only: Florence is a frontend for NetSurf, whose core is GPL-2.0-only, and the browser
is a single executable that links it; several files here are also derived from NetSurf's own
frontends (frontend/gs_schedule.*, gs_filetype.*, gs_fetch.*, gs_core.c, gs_plot.c, Makefile*), whose
copyright holders are NetSurf's contributors.

Copyright (c) 2026 Anurodh Pokharel for the files that carry no other copyright notice.

Exceptions, which keep their own terms:
  configs/curl/curl_config.h   curl's licence (it is curl's configuration header)
  tools/bind_audit.sh          vendored from the xnu-iokit-pi3 port; its licence is that repo's

Third-party sources that setup_third_party.sh fetches (NetSurf and its libraries, mbedTLS, curl,
libjpeg, nsgenbind, the CA bundle) keep their own licences. Each source file carries an
SPDX-License-Identifier line that is authoritative for that file.
